86311754 1145 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5x-3y-8 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x)+({y}^{2}-3y) & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & =8+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{33}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{33}{2} \\\\ {(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}.$" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311756 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311757 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311758 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311759 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311760 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1041 "selection" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311759 13194139534814 true] [17592186311755 1110 #uuid "c9590550-298d-5252-851f-963e24812c3c" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311756 1034 "center: $(-\\frac{5}{2},-\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534814 true] [17592186311756 1111 #uuid "6ec723b9-8fdd-5b90-ab8c-cc1c07e3fd25" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311757 1034 "center: $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}),$ radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{33}{2}}$" 13194139534814 true] [17592186311757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534814 true] [17592186311757 1111 #uuid "a613efdf-e165-500e-9338-a519b